  "title": "AI Search - Manage AI Search instances in any namespace with Terraform",
  "content": "<p>Starting with <a href=\"https://registry.terraform.io/providers/cloudflare/cloudflare/latest/docs\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Cloudflare Terraform provider<span class=\"external-link\"> ↗︎</span></a> v5.29.0, you can manage <a href=\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/ai-search/\">AI Search</a> instances in any <a href=\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/ai-search/concepts/namespaces/\">namespace</a>, not only <code>default</code>.</p>\n<p>The <code>cloudflare_ai_search_instance</code> resource has a new <code>namespace</code> argument. It defaults to <code>default</code>, so existing configurations keep managing the same instances.</p>\n<figure class=\"nb-code-figure\"><pre class=\"astro-code astro-code-themes github-light github-dark nb-shiki-c6xiwz\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"nb-shiki-1t8gfj\">resource</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-dzsirb\"> \"cloudflare_ai_search_namespace\"</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-dzsirb\"> \"support\"</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-140thh\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"nb-shiki-140thh\">  account_id</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-1itgoe\"> =</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-140thh\"> var</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-1itgoe\">.</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-140thh\">account_id</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"nb-shiki-140thh\">  name</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-1itgoe\">       =</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-mdbnqw\"> \"support\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"nb-shiki-140thh\">}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"nb-shiki-1t8gfj\">resource</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-dzsirb\"> \"cloudflare_ai_search_instance\"</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-dzsirb\"> \"docs\"</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-140thh\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"nb-shiki-140thh\">  account_id</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-1itgoe\"> =</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-140thh\"> var</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-1itgoe\">.</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-140thh\">account_id</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"nb-shiki-140thh\">  id</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-1itgoe\">         =</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-mdbnqw\"> \"docs\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"nb-shiki-140thh\">  namespace</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-1itgoe\">  =</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-140thh\"> cloudflare_ai_search_namespace</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-1itgoe\">.</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-140thh\">support</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-1itgoe\">.</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-140thh\">name</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"nb-shiki-140thh\">}</span></span></code></pre></figure>\n<p>You can import existing instances and namespaces:</p>\n<figure class=\"nb-code-figure\"><pre class=\"astro-code astro-code-themes github-light github-dark nb-shiki-c6xiwz\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"nb-shiki-1t8gfj\">terraform</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-mdbnqw\"> import</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-mdbnqw\"> cloudflare_ai_search_instance.docs</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-1itgoe\"> &lt;</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-mdbnqw\">account_i</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-140thh\">d</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-1itgoe\">&gt;</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-mdbnqw\">/support/docs</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"nb-shiki-1t8gfj\">terraform</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-mdbnqw\"> import</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-mdbnqw\"> cloudflare_ai_search_namespace.support</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-1itgoe\"> &lt;</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-mdbnqw\">account_i</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-140thh\">d</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-1itgoe\">&gt;</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-mdbnqw\">/support</span></span></code></pre></figure>\n<p>The data sources read instances from the namespace you set:</p>\n<figure class=\"nb-code-figure\"><pre class=\"astro-code astro-code-themes github-light github-dark nb-shiki-c6xiwz\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"nb-shiki-1t8gfj\">data</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-dzsirb\"> \"cloudflare_ai_search_instance\"</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-dzsirb\"> \"docs\"</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-140thh\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"nb-shiki-140thh\">  account_id</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-1itgoe\"> =</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-140thh\"> var</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-1itgoe\">.</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-140thh\">account_id</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"nb-shiki-140thh\">  namespace</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-1itgoe\">  =</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-mdbnqw\"> \"support\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"nb-shiki-140thh\">  id</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-1itgoe\">         =</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-mdbnqw\"> \"docs\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"nb-shiki-140thh\">}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"nb-shiki-1t8gfj\">data</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-dzsirb\"> \"cloudflare_ai_search_instances\"</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-dzsirb\"> \"support\"</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-140thh\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"nb-shiki-140thh\">  account_id</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-1itgoe\"> =</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-140thh\"> var</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-1itgoe\">.</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-140thh\">account_id</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"nb-shiki-140thh\">  namespace</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-1itgoe\">  =</span><span class=\"nb-shiki-mdbnqw\"> \"support\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"nb-shiki-140thh\">}</span></span></code></pre></figure>\n<p>When you upgrade to v5.29.0, review these changes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The <code>cloudflare_ai_search_instance</code> import ID now includes the namespace: <code>&lt;account_id&gt;/&lt;namespace&gt;/&lt;id&gt;</code>. For instances in the default namespace, use <code>&lt;account_id&gt;/default/&lt;id&gt;</code>.</li>\n<li>The <code>cloudflare_ai_search_instance</code> and <code>cloudflare_ai_search_instances</code> data sources require <code>namespace</code>. Set <code>namespace = \"default\"</code> for instances in the default namespace.</li>\n<li><code>cloudflare_ai_search_instances</code> returns the instances in one namespace. The <code>filter.namespace</code> argument of <code>cloudflare_ai_search_instance</code> is removed.</li>\n<li>Changing <code>namespace</code> replaces the instance.</li>\n</ul>",
